AU  - Liu, J
AU  - Zhang, DD
AU  - Xiang, GP
AU  - Xu, XN
TI  - Spatiotemporal dynamics and driving factors of aboveground biomass in the Zoige grasslands
T2  - ECOLOGICAL FRONTIERS
AB  - Alpine grasslands play an important role in sustaining ecosystem functions, and understanding their dynamic trajectories and associated drivers is critical for effective conservation and sustainable management. We investigated the spatiotemporal dynamics of aboveground biomass (AGB) in the Zoige alpine grasslands from 2000 to 2019 and identified its dominant driving factors by utilizing multi-source data, combined with temporal spectral segmentation and relative importance analysis. Our results reveal that between 2000 and 2019, AGB exhibited a modest overall increase (0.33 g m-2 yr-1); however, localized AGB loss events remained frequent, posing risks to regional ecosystem stability. AGB dynamics were driven by a combination of climatic and anthropogenic factors, with temperature and precipitation serving as primary drivers in 31.73 % and 22.60% of the grassland area, respectively. Grazing pressure and population density accounted for 21.01 % and 19.80%, respectively. Our results provide a theoretical basis for identifying degradation hotspots in Zoige grasslands and for developing scientifically informed restoration strategies.
